## Why This Is Asked
This question probes how to architect robust, scalable, and private multi-tenant routing for LLMs with shared infrastructure, covering isolation, governance, and latency.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant adapters
- Data locality and provenance
- Drift detection and safety gates
- Latency SLAs and auditing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-routing sketch
function route(request, tenant) {
  const adapter = getAdapter(tenant);
  const tagged = tagProvenance(request, tenant);
  if(!policyAllows(tagged, adapter)) throw new Error("Forbidden");
  return adapter.forwardToModel(tagged);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale isolation as tenants scale? 
- What metrics and tests ensure drift is detected early?

## Why This Is Asked
Assess ability to design governance-aware, low-latency LLM gating in multi-tenant contexts with compliance, verifiable provenance, and drift detection.

## Key Concepts
- Policy schema design for strict data governance
- Real-time evaluation and routing with canary semantics
- Tamper-evident logging and prompt hashing
- Drift and latency testing in distributed infra

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple policy eval skeleton
function evaluatePolicy(prompt, policy) {
  const redacted = applyRedaction(prompt, policy.redaction_rules);
  const hash = hashPrompt(redacted, policy);
  const allowed = policy.allowed;
  return { allowed, redacted, hash };
}
```

