- How would you ensure logs remain tamper-evident during partial outages?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design dynamic, policy-driven routing with on-edge latency constraints, multi-tenant safeguards, and auditable provenance. It also probes risk scoring, drift detection, and rollback semantics under real-world operational pressures.

## Key Concepts

- Contextual bandits for real-time routing decisions
- Per-tenant safety profiles and data locality constraints
- Latency budgets and SLA adherence (p95 targets)
- Drift detection and automated rollback to baseline
- Tamper-evident, cryptographically signed per-tenant audit logs

## Code Example

```javascript
function selectVariant(context, stats) {
  // context: {tenant, latency, safetyProfile}
  // stats: {risk, base, tuned, safety}
  if (Math.random() < 0.1) return 'base';
  if (stats.risk > 0.6) return 'safety-guarded';
  const scores = { base: stats.base, tuned: stats.tuned, safety: stats.safety };
  return Object.keys(scores).reduce((a,b) => scores[a] > scores[b] ? a : b);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you prevent feedback loops from online learning contaminating production signals?
- What telemetry and signing strategy ensures tamper resistance without leaking tenant data?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of per-tenant privacy controls, simple API design, and ingest-time auditing with a concrete example.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant policy and versioning
- Regex-based redaction and field-level redaction
- Lightweight audit logging without storing raw prompts

## Code Example

```javascript
function sanitizePrompt(tenantPolicy, prompt) {
  let redacted = prompt;
  for (const r of tenantPolicy.redactRegexes) {
    redacted = redacted.replace(new RegExp(r, 'g'), '[REDACTED]');
  }
  tenantPolicy.redactFields.forEach(f => {
    const re = new RegExp(`"${f}"\s*:\s*"[^"]*"`, 'g');
    redacted = redacted.replace(re, `"${f}":"[REDACTED]"`);
  });
  return redacted;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test performance under bursty load?
- How would policy updates drift affect in-flight requests and how would you mitigate?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests auditing, determinism, and privacy within a simple llm-ops workflow, ensuring a practical path to compliant replays without exposing raw data.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant-scoped versioning
- Deterministic hashing with per-tenant salt
- Audit replay API and sandboxed execution
- Privacy: store hashes, not raw prompts/outputs
- Version retention and storage strategy

## Code Example

```typescript
import crypto from 'crypto';
function hashPrompt(input: string, salt: string): string {
  const h = crypto.createHmac('sha256', salt);
  h.update(input);
  return h.digest('hex');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you purge old versions?
- How would you test for hash collisions and replay fidelity?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to implement low-latency, per-tenant policy gating with live hot-swaps, immutability guarantees, and rollback strategies in a production LLM-ops gateway.

## Key Concepts

- Per-brand policy isolation and versioning
- Immutable policy versions with blue/green rollout
- Fast policy evaluation (sub-20 ms) and robust auditing
- WASM/Rust prototype for safe, sandboxed evaluation

## Code Example

```rust
// Minimal WASM-friendly policy evaluator API
pub fn eval(input: &str, policy_json: &str) -> bool {
    // naive policy: blocklist example
    if policy_json.contains("blocked") {
        return !input.contains("blocked");
    }
    true
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you monitor policy drift and trigger automatic rollbacks?
- What metrics would you collect to ensure low false negatives with high safety?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design adaptive residency and tenancy policy in a real multi-tenant LLM gateway, handling regulatory events, drift alerts, and auditable changes.

## Key Concepts
- Policy as code with per-tenant residency and retention rules
- Dynamic tenancy routing and hot-updatable policies
- Drift detection, versioning, rollback, and tamper-evident auditing
- API design, data models, and test coverage

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal policy model (JS-like)
function TenantPolicy(tenantId, residency, retentionDays, piiHandling, version, lastUpdated) {
  this.tenantId = tenantId;
  this.residency = residency; // 'on-prem'|'private-cloud'|'shared'
  this.retentionDays = retentionDays;
  this.piiHandling = piiHandling; // 'redact'|'anonymize'|'allow'
  this.version = version;
  this.lastUpdated = lastUpdated;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement drift detection and rollback strategy?
- What metrics and tests validate residency switches without SLA breach?
